usage: dashboard-preview.py [-h] [--rc RC] [--prefix PREFIX] [--port PORT] [--mock MOCK]
                            [--auto-mock] [--reader Reader.java] [--live BASE_URL]
                            [--config-login] [--config-password CONFIG_PASSWORD]
                            [--config-ttl CONFIG_TTL] [--editor]

Local preview server for a Niagara dashboard -ux module.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --rc RC               path to the module's rc/ folder (default ./src/rc)
  --prefix PREFIX       servlet mount prefix (default /dashboardpan)
  --port PORT           port (default 8080)
  --mock MOCK           JSON file served for every GET /api/<name> (default: empty {})
  --auto-mock           generate equipment mock by parsing the module's *Reader.java; mutually
                        exclusive with --mock and --live
  --reader Reader.java  path to the *Reader.java when using --auto-mock; if omitted the file is
                        auto-located under the sibling src/ of --rc
  --live BASE_URL       proxy /api/* GETs AND POSTs (writes) to BASE_URL/<prefix>/api/* (real
                        station), relaying the station status code; mutually exclusive with --mock
                        and --auto-mock
  --config-login        preview the R14 'second login before any write' flow: injects a native
                        modal + session chip + change_log strip and adds stateful
                        /config/login|logout|session mock endpoints; writes need a session
  --config-password CONFIG_PASSWORD
                        demo password accepted by the mock login (default 1234)
  --config-ttl CONFIG_TTL
                        mock config-session TTL in seconds, sliding (default 300 = the HMI product
                        default, lead 2026-09-06)
  --editor              inject a preview-only label editor (drag points/labels, export
                        rx/ry/rlx/rly/rside); never touches the module rc/
